after:
These records show checks on a summary before and after a change. true means the check passed. The code counts recorded results; it does not test a model.

```javascript
const before = { mainPoint: true, date: true, name: false };
const after = { mainPoint: true, date: false, name: true };
console.log(Object.values(before).filter(Boolean).length);
console.log(Object.values(after).filter(Boolean).length);
```

It prints 2, then 2. Object.values takes the recorded values, and filter(Boolean) keeps the true ones here.
